sentences.t:
Interea ad templum non aequae Palladis ibant
crinibus Iliades passis peplumque ferebant,
suppliciter tristes et tunsae pectora palmis;

sentences.l:
Meanwhile to the temple of unkind Pallas went
the Trojan women with loosened hair, and they carried a robe,
suppliantly sad, and beaten on their breasts with their palms;

sentences.t:
Dissimulant, et nube cava speculantur amicti,
quae fortuna viris, classem quo litore linquant,
quid veniant;

sentences.l:
They hide their feelings, and wrapped in the hollow cloud they watch
what fortune is for the men, on what shore they are leaving the fleet,
why they come;

sentences.t:
Quem si fata virum servant, si vescitur aura
aetheria, neque adhuc crudelibus occubat umbris,
non metus;

sentences.l:
Which man, if the fates keep him safe, if he feeds on the air
of heaven, and does not yet lie in the cruel shades,
there is no fear;
